WEBVTT

00:01:40.240 --> 00:01:43.910
For appetizers, we'll have the
assortment of seasonal vegetables...

00:01:43.910 --> 00:01:47.380
and the escargot-style littleneck
clams in garlic butter sauce.

00:01:47.380 --> 00:01:50.550
And then the homestyle meat pie.

00:01:50.550 --> 00:01:52.820
For pasta, we'll have penne with Gorgonzola.

00:01:52.820 --> 00:01:54.910
And for the main course, Ibérico pork roast.

00:01:56.520 --> 00:01:58.090
Will that do?

00:01:58.090 --> 00:01:59.490
Fine with me.

00:01:59.490 --> 00:02:01.060
Any drinks?

00:02:01.060 --> 00:02:02.290
No. We're fine.

00:02:02.290 --> 00:02:04.020
As you wish, sir.

00:02:04.300 --> 00:02:08.300
I never knew Maihama had a restaurant like this.

00:02:08.300 --> 00:02:09.960
Shizuno.

00:02:10.400 --> 00:02:14.040
You know why I asked you here tonight.

00:02:14.040 --> 00:02:19.040
But, I... As to why I invited you...

00:02:19.040 --> 00:02:21.770
I'd like to know the reason.

00:02:25.650 --> 00:02:28.210
I wonder if these flowers are artificial.

00:02:28.790 --> 00:02:32.350
Although perhaps you can't call
any flowers in this world "fresh."

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:36.130
Where did you go this morning?

00:02:36.130 --> 00:02:38.230
Questions so soon?

00:02:38.230 --> 00:02:40.960
Weren't we going to enjoy a tasty meal first?

00:02:41.170 --> 00:02:44.660
You're the one who will decide the flavor of this meal.

00:02:47.640 --> 00:02:49.440
This morning?

00:03:06.260 --> 00:03:08.730
Transfer data to server control block.

00:03:17.640 --> 00:03:19.540
I don't remember.

00:03:20.610 --> 00:03:22.600
Please don't play dumb.

00:03:23.310 --> 00:03:24.580
It happened this morning!

00:03:24.580 --> 00:03:26.040
Ah...

00:03:26.040 --> 00:03:28.410
I recall being at the pool, watching Kyo.

00:03:51.240 --> 00:03:53.070
Disgraceful, isn't he?

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.140
Yeah. Disgraceful.

00:03:55.140 --> 00:03:56.270
You got a point to make?

00:03:56.270 --> 00:03:57.640
Shut up!

00:03:57.640 --> 00:04:01.270
Look at you, struggling all
alone to reform the swim club!

00:04:04.180 --> 00:04:05.340
You son of a!

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:08.650
Hey!

00:04:09.020 --> 00:04:10.010
What?!

00:04:12.160 --> 00:04:14.030
What would you do?

00:04:14.030 --> 00:04:16.260
What would you do
if you became a real person?

00:04:19.660 --> 00:04:23.830
It'll feel nice to get out of here
and become real people, won't it?

00:04:24.470 --> 00:04:27.070
What do you mean "a real person?!"

00:04:27.070 --> 00:04:30.180
What are we now? Dogs and cats?

00:04:30.180 --> 00:04:31.970
Or maybe we're ghosts?

00:04:32.580 --> 00:04:35.210
The world's nothing but ruins out there,

00:04:35.210 --> 00:04:37.680
but I think you guys
would be able to survive!

00:04:38.120 --> 00:04:40.610
Quit babbling at us!

00:04:44.490 --> 00:04:45.850
The guy's gone nuts!

00:04:50.460 --> 00:04:52.430
I don't know how long it'll take,

00:04:52.830 --> 00:04:55.070
but until the day
we can be resurrected,

00:04:55.070 --> 00:04:57.500
we'll protect it. Maihama...

00:05:02.640 --> 00:05:04.130
Right, Kaminagi?

00:05:08.480 --> 00:05:11.010
He's very positive now.

00:05:11.920 --> 00:05:16.350
He believes the day will come when
he'll be able to pick a real flower.

00:05:16.590 --> 00:05:18.850
Don't try to change the subject.

00:05:20.390 --> 00:05:23.830
Your escargot-style littleneck
clams in garlic butter sauce, sir.

00:05:24.460 --> 00:05:28.190
You'll find that soaking up the remaining
sauce with your bread is very tasty.

00:05:28.700 --> 00:05:29.690
Thank you.

00:05:30.940 --> 00:05:34.070
At 10:17 local time, unencrypted data...

00:05:34.070 --> 00:05:40.480
of the location of the Maihama server
was transmitted via the satellite network.

00:05:41.110 --> 00:05:44.820
The sender is unknown.
The source is also unknown.

00:05:44.820 --> 00:05:46.620
May-yu picked up the signal by chance...

00:05:46.620 --> 00:05:48.850
while she was doing
maintenance on the Garuda.

00:05:49.890 --> 00:05:53.150
We've received reports that other
ships picked up the signal as well.

00:05:55.330 --> 00:05:57.800
Who did it?

00:05:57.800 --> 00:05:59.130
Who knows?

00:06:00.430 --> 00:06:02.660
We should probably accept
that we've been found out.

00:06:03.200 --> 00:06:05.190
The location of the Maihama server?!

00:06:06.370 --> 00:06:08.840
As far as they're concerned,
the Maihama server...

00:06:08.910 --> 00:06:13.900
is a nuisance that's been mass-producing
new Cerebrants around here lately.

00:06:14.510 --> 00:06:18.020
I figured it was just a matter
of time before it was targeted.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:19.850
Are they coming now?!

00:06:20.820 --> 00:06:22.950
Where's Lu-shen and Shizuno-sempai?!

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.120
And where are May-yu and May-yen?!

00:06:25.420 --> 00:06:27.060
They've gone off-line.

00:06:27.060 --> 00:06:28.790
We can't contact them.

00:06:29.360 --> 00:06:30.450
They've gone missing?!

00:06:33.200 --> 00:06:34.760
Commander Shima!

00:06:36.940 --> 00:06:40.100
You've been told the details.
Your orders, sir?

00:06:41.470 --> 00:06:42.730
We stand by.

00:06:44.540 --> 00:06:47.310
Are you kidding?!
They're after our city!

00:06:49.180 --> 00:06:50.720
What is it?

00:06:50.720 --> 00:06:53.410
I've picked up readings of
Gards-orm quantum weaponry!

00:06:54.190 --> 00:06:56.280
They're approaching Maihama.

00:07:01.130 --> 00:07:04.330
Ruins... Relics of the past.

00:07:04.330 --> 00:07:07.460
Yes. There's no need for them now.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:11.300
At last, one of our battles will end.

00:07:11.300 --> 00:07:13.600
That's right, Abyss.

00:07:14.670 --> 00:07:17.000
Here they come!
I'll head out and stop them!

00:07:18.810 --> 00:07:20.180
I suppose.

00:07:21.350 --> 00:07:23.110
Why are you acting like this is nothing?!

00:07:24.480 --> 00:07:26.380
Why, when the Maihama server's in danger?!

00:07:31.460 --> 00:07:32.390
Kyo!

00:07:32.790 --> 00:07:34.280
Right! Let's go!

00:07:35.260 --> 00:07:39.390
<i>Gunner and Wizard I.D.s, locked in.</i>
<i>Stand by for meta-body transmission!</i>

00:07:39.660 --> 00:07:43.620
<i>Chamber seals, released.</i>
<i>Q.L. driver, conjunction.</i>

00:07:44.400 --> 00:07:46.460
<i>Restoration coordinates, set and locked!</i>

00:07:46.870 --> 00:07:47.800
Entangle!

00:08:13.870 --> 00:08:16.490
The Altair has engaged the Coatlicue.

00:08:19.540 --> 00:08:22.610
So, who sent that unidentified signal?

00:08:22.610 --> 00:08:24.810
The ones we suspect of doing it...

00:08:24.810 --> 00:08:29.080
are either you
or Commander Shima.

00:08:29.510 --> 00:08:31.240
And your reasoning for that?

00:08:31.950 --> 00:08:35.250
We found traces that some of
the data had been deleted...

00:08:35.250 --> 00:08:37.690
from the activity log data for
the Oceanus's remaining crew.

00:08:38.460 --> 00:08:39.860
I see.

00:08:40.260 --> 00:08:44.090
This morning, you entered
the Maihama server. Correct?

00:08:44.460 --> 00:08:46.630
You've done a lot of checking up on me.

00:08:46.630 --> 00:08:48.960
But why would I do it?

00:08:51.040 --> 00:08:52.830
That's what I want to know.

00:08:54.210 --> 00:08:56.610
If I told you that neither I nor Shima did it,

00:08:56.610 --> 00:08:58.770
could we just end this
sudden dinner date?

00:08:59.740 --> 00:09:02.210
Kyo is waiting. If you'll excuse me.

00:09:02.210 --> 00:09:05.270
Have a seat.
There's more food to come.

00:09:09.420 --> 00:09:12.120
Forgive me, but I've locked your cereb-icon.

00:09:15.830 --> 00:09:20.030
I doubt the Maihama server
will be destroyed so easily.

00:09:20.030 --> 00:09:24.470
I believe it was constructed to
withstand even a nuclear attack.

00:09:25.200 --> 00:09:28.140
Even the Anti-Zega will find it difficult to get in.

00:09:29.010 --> 00:09:30.600
I'm sure.

00:09:30.980 --> 00:09:33.310
And as long as the person suspected...

00:09:33.310 --> 00:09:37.810
of passing the server's location
to the enemy is still inside of it...

00:09:39.120 --> 00:09:41.610
then there's no way they'd destroy it.

00:09:49.730 --> 00:09:52.160
Kyo, they got past us!

00:09:52.560 --> 00:09:55.900
Where the hell is Lu-shen?!
Where's Shizuno-sempai?!

00:09:56.870 --> 00:09:58.300
No one's coming...

00:09:58.800 --> 00:10:00.960
No one from the Oceanus is coming.

00:10:01.570 --> 00:10:04.610
They've written off our Maihama server!

00:10:04.610 --> 00:10:05.580
DAMN THEM!

00:10:13.380 --> 00:10:14.510
Found it!

00:10:17.920 --> 00:10:19.820
There's the hive.

00:10:20.660 --> 00:10:21.750
I won't let you go!

00:10:34.840 --> 00:10:36.710
Coatlicue closing on the Maihama server!

00:10:36.710 --> 00:10:38.710
Commander, I'm going out!

00:10:38.710 --> 00:10:41.750
Even you would have no chance
out there without a Wizard!

00:10:41.750 --> 00:10:43.210
We stand by!

00:10:43.350 --> 00:10:44.450
But, sir!

00:10:44.450 --> 00:10:48.980
Everyone, do as the commander says!
He must have some kind of idea!

00:10:53.790 --> 00:10:54.950
He must...

00:11:03.430 --> 00:11:04.640
What happened?

00:11:04.640 --> 00:11:06.500
They've penetrated it!

00:11:06.940 --> 00:11:08.140
I won't let them!

00:11:08.140 --> 00:11:11.240
Our city... Maihama...

00:11:11.240 --> 00:11:13.140
I won't let them destroy it!

00:11:18.820 --> 00:11:21.050
Maihama will not fall.

00:11:21.050 --> 00:11:23.450
What if you've guessed wrong?

00:11:24.320 --> 00:11:26.820
It'll all disappear. This city here...

00:11:26.820 --> 00:11:28.290
And you with it.

00:11:29.790 --> 00:11:32.020
I'll have my answer soon.

00:11:57.690 --> 00:12:00.560
No response! How far did they get in?!

00:12:00.860 --> 00:12:02.930
If they get through the
manufacturing machine tunnels,

00:12:02.930 --> 00:12:05.120
it looks like they'd get all the
way down to the deepest levels.

00:12:12.240 --> 00:12:13.400
Bastard!

00:12:13.400 --> 00:12:17.310
Kyo... We should be prepared
to not get any reinforcements.

00:12:18.010 --> 00:12:19.870
I'm not expecting any.

00:12:20.280 --> 00:12:23.980
The only ones who want to defend the Maihama
server from the bottom of their hearts is us!

00:12:26.250 --> 00:12:27.620
Some day...

00:12:27.620 --> 00:12:31.420
Some day, we'll all be real people
again and we'll stand on the Earth!

00:12:32.260 --> 00:12:35.560
We'll a create a world for
our Maihama to exist in, too!

00:12:35.560 --> 00:12:37.530
Until then, we'll protect it!

00:12:39.130 --> 00:12:40.390
And so...

00:12:40.900 --> 00:12:42.390
Let's do this!

00:12:49.610 --> 00:12:51.440
They're approaching the server?

00:12:52.040 --> 00:12:54.340
We're in trouble, aren't we?
It should be soon.

00:12:57.580 --> 00:13:01.140
I really do want to contact Kyo.
Please let me go.

00:13:01.990 --> 00:13:06.150
Do you really still want to be
sitting in Kyo's rear seat again?

00:13:07.530 --> 00:13:10.190
I know you and he used
to have a relationship.

00:13:12.360 --> 00:13:15.160
I still love him, even now.

00:13:15.500 --> 00:13:17.970
And so, what? You're jealous?

00:13:18.640 --> 00:13:21.470
Surely that wouldn't drive you
to destroy everything!

00:13:21.470 --> 00:13:24.570
As grateful as I am for it,
I'm not <i>that</i> emotional.

00:13:25.280 --> 00:13:27.900
It's because he was the one who saved me.

00:13:28.680 --> 00:13:30.010
So...

00:13:30.580 --> 00:13:32.640
What are you after, then?

00:13:41.260 --> 00:13:43.830
Stop deceiving Kyo.

00:13:43.830 --> 00:13:46.320
He's had enough pain in his life.

00:13:47.570 --> 00:13:51.760
It would be awful if he had to find
out about your part in this betrayal.

00:13:59.680 --> 00:14:02.040
Isn't it time for the main course?

00:14:17.860 --> 00:14:18.730
What the?

00:14:18.730 --> 00:14:21.220
This is video from
the Maihama server room.

00:14:21.670 --> 00:14:25.540
The quantum computer is designed
to do this in response to an intruder!

00:14:25.540 --> 00:14:26.940
Got him!

00:14:27.340 --> 00:14:28.670
What?

00:14:35.980 --> 00:14:37.950
And here is the nest itself.

00:14:38.350 --> 00:14:40.380
It is from here that the eggs are laid.

00:14:40.380 --> 00:14:42.220
And then the eggs hatch into birds.

00:14:43.050 --> 00:14:45.390
And all we need do now is smash it.

00:15:06.080 --> 00:15:08.980
What's wrong? Just touch it!

00:15:13.080 --> 00:15:16.210
But... This is just too easy.

00:15:21.290 --> 00:15:22.530
We made it!

00:15:22.530 --> 00:15:23.750
The server's still safe!

00:15:34.470 --> 00:15:36.130
<i>Kyo Sogoru! Well done!</i>

00:15:37.010 --> 00:15:39.510
<i>Enough! Leave him alone!</i>
<i>Let him do it!</i>

00:15:39.510 --> 00:15:41.610
What are you saying?!

00:15:41.610 --> 00:15:43.580
<i>If we let him touch the server itself,</i>

00:15:43.580 --> 00:15:47.450
<i>we'll be able to extract all the data on him!</i>
<i>That's the trap we set!</i>

00:15:47.690 --> 00:15:49.380
What do you mean?!

00:15:49.750 --> 00:15:53.690
If you use the giant quantum computer
here that the Oceanus doesn't have,

00:15:53.690 --> 00:15:56.320
then you would be able to collect
all the data on the Anti-Zega.

00:15:56.990 --> 00:15:59.490
What?! That's impossible...

00:16:00.330 --> 00:16:03.330
<i>And for that, you'd destroy Maihama?</i>

00:16:03.330 --> 00:16:06.390
<i>You'd sacrifice Tomigai and</i>
<i>Kawaguchi and everyone else?!</i>

00:16:09.110 --> 00:16:12.800
What better bait for the enemy than the
server that's giving them so much trouble?

00:16:14.380 --> 00:16:15.850
You bastard!

00:16:17.380 --> 00:16:20.250
You mean the location of the
Maihama server was leaked to them...

00:16:20.250 --> 00:16:23.380
to lure the Anti-Zega into a trap?!

00:16:25.220 --> 00:16:26.550
Exactly.

00:16:27.420 --> 00:16:30.860
And sending the Altair out...
Kyo's intercepting them was...

00:16:31.360 --> 00:16:33.090
To make it look real.

00:16:35.000 --> 00:16:38.870
Even if it was necessary to deceive
your own side for this operation,

00:16:38.870 --> 00:16:43.030
on what basis did the Gards-orm
believe you so completely?

00:16:43.570 --> 00:16:45.170
Who knows?

00:16:46.010 --> 00:16:49.970
You and Shima have some sort of
a relationship with the Gards-orm.

00:16:50.980 --> 00:16:52.880
Don't you?

00:16:57.390 --> 00:17:00.450
<i>Listen to me! Direct contact</i>
<i>with the server acts as a switch.</i>

00:17:00.690 --> 00:17:03.850
<i>When activated, the quantum computer</i>
<i>will begin scanning the Coatlicue!</i>

00:17:04.330 --> 00:17:06.130
<i>Push him into the server!</i>

00:17:06.130 --> 00:17:07.530
I said I can't do that!

00:17:07.870 --> 00:17:09.200
This is an order!

00:17:09.200 --> 00:17:10.430
Kyo...

00:17:10.430 --> 00:17:12.100
How can I do it?!

00:17:14.040 --> 00:17:18.480
If the server is destroyed, then Maihama...
Everyone will disappear!

00:17:18.910 --> 00:17:20.880
Don't lose this chance, Kyo!

00:17:24.420 --> 00:17:26.440
Kyo, we can do it.

00:17:27.050 --> 00:17:29.380
This Zega... In the Altair's fist...

00:17:29.920 --> 00:17:33.520
If I reconfigure the giant quantum
computer transceiver in there,

00:17:33.520 --> 00:17:36.460
we can do this through your fist,
without touching the server!

00:17:38.630 --> 00:17:40.190
With this?!

00:17:40.600 --> 00:17:41.860
Hurry, before he realizes!

00:17:42.130 --> 00:17:45.620
<i>Right arm has converted to transceiver functionality.</i>

00:17:47.270 --> 00:17:47.930
Do it!

00:17:53.310 --> 00:17:55.440
Running away now?!

00:17:57.250 --> 00:17:59.040
- Dammit!
- Keep calm!

00:17:59.850 --> 00:18:01.350
You can do this, Kyo!

00:18:01.350 --> 00:18:02.550
R- Right!

00:18:07.120 --> 00:18:08.590
Lightless ones!

00:18:08.590 --> 00:18:10.320
Time to return to nothingness!

00:18:22.540 --> 00:18:24.010
Deeper! Push it in deeper!

00:18:37.690 --> 00:18:39.780
We've breached the enemy's firewall!

00:18:41.190 --> 00:18:42.830
What have they done?!

00:18:42.830 --> 00:18:43.690
Abyss!

00:18:43.960 --> 00:18:45.360
You son of a!

00:19:06.250 --> 00:19:07.520
What's wrong?!

00:19:07.520 --> 00:19:09.720
The cable that the Anti-Zega is holding...

00:19:09.720 --> 00:19:13.660
is connected to the Maihama server's
lowest-level quantum conversion reactor!

00:19:14.860 --> 00:19:18.560
If he makes it lose control,
the Maihama server will be destroyed!

00:19:22.900 --> 00:19:25.270
What? He's trying to self-destruct?!

00:19:25.270 --> 00:19:26.340
<i>Get out of there!</i>

00:19:26.340 --> 00:19:27.840
Are you kidding?!

00:19:27.840 --> 00:19:31.000
There's no time!
Do you want to get blown up?!

00:19:31.380 --> 00:19:34.110
Kyo! I want to stay with you!

00:19:34.110 --> 00:19:36.310
Same here. But...

00:19:36.310 --> 00:19:38.440
I have to protect them all!

00:19:41.790 --> 00:19:44.250
We're all going to be human again!

00:19:48.830 --> 00:19:50.590
Force transmission of the Altair!

00:19:58.300 --> 00:19:59.230
What?!

00:20:28.400 --> 00:20:30.700
Maihama is!

00:20:30.700 --> 00:20:32.030
Oh, Kyo!

00:20:57.330 --> 00:21:01.490
The Maihama server was destroyed, and yet...

00:21:05.200 --> 00:21:06.900
We didn't disappear.

00:21:06.900 --> 00:21:09.100
What's the meaning of this?!

00:21:10.640 --> 00:21:13.410
I think I'll have dessert.

00:22:51.710 --> 00:22:53.540
Am I dreaming?!

00:22:53.540 --> 00:22:57.110
Everything and everyone is just fine!
What the hell's going on?!

00:22:57.110 --> 00:22:59.120
You know why, don't you, Sempai?!

00:22:59.120 --> 00:23:05.260
I know. Only Shima and I know the
terrible secret about the Maihama server.

00:23:05.260 --> 00:23:06.260
You mean?

00:23:06.260 --> 00:23:12.130
Yes. We exist in the safest and also the
most dangerous place for humanity.

00:23:12.130 --> 00:23:15.870
Next time, on Zegapain: "Yehl, Shizuno."

00:23:15.870 --> 00:23:18.970
My pain, never to be forgotten.
